hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"500","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, from Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Hanan, from Abu Uthman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is given sweet basil, let him not refuse it, for it has come out of Paradise."
